* A: bipolar op amp with an npn input pair, +/-15 V
* pins: inp inn vcc vee out
.subckt OPA_NPN inp inn vcc vee out
* tail: npn current source 20 uA to vee
Q10 t b10 r10 QN
R10 r10 vee 10k
Q11 b10 b10 r11 QN
R11 r11 vee 10k
Ib  vcc b10 20u
* input pair (inn on Q1, inp on Q2) with pnp mirror load
Q1 c1 inn t QN
Q2 c2 inp t QN
Q3 c1 c1 vcc QP
Q4 c2 c1 vcc QP
* second stage: pnp common emitter, Miller capacitor, current-source load
Q5 o2 c2 vcc QP
Cc c2 o2 30p
Q12 ob b12 r12 QN 10
R12 r12 vee 1k
* separate bias for Q12, so that its saturation cannot starve the tail mirror
Ib2 vcc b12 20u
Q13 b12 b12 r13 QN
R13 r13 vee 10k
* class-AB output with two bias diodes
D1 o2 m DD
D2 m ob DD
Q7 vcc o2 e7 QN 10
Q8 vee ob e8 QP 10
R7 e7 out 25
R8 e8 out 25
.ends
